// Owned by Sunshine's prep-cmd (mySunshine.captureOutput) — REWRITTEN at every
// stream start and stop. Seeded here so the include always resolves; the live
// copy is writable and diverges, so this is seed/ rather than dots/.
//
// Why a file and not `niri msg output`: those are TRANSIENT changes, and niri
// throws transient output config away on any config reload where the file's
// output section differs from the last load (niri.rs, reload_config). DMS
// regenerates dms/outputs.kdl at runtime, so a stream could lose its output
// mid-session and windows would silently fall back to the desktop monitor.
// File state survives reloads.
output "HDMI-A-1" {
    off
}
